- =deploy.sh:14= — =git stash pop= runs unconditionally, but =git stash= (line 3) only creates a stash if there were changes.
- With a clean tree, =pop= either fails or pops an unrelated older stash.
- Guard by only popping if a stash was actually pushed (e.g., =git stash push -m deploy= + check).


